---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site collects, what it doesn't, and why there is no cookie banner."
>
  <main class="reading" id="main">
    <section class="block insight-page">
      <p class="kicker">TROi</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>

      <p class="privacy-lede">
        Short version: this site sets no cookies, builds no profile of you, and there is nothing here to
        consent to. The longer version is below, because saying so without showing the working is exactly
        the kind of thing nobody should take at face value.
      </p>

      <h2>No cookies</h2>
      <p>
        The site sets no cookies at all — not for analytics, not for preferences, not for anything else.
        That is why you are not being asked to accept any. A banner asking permission to do nothing would be
        theatre.
      </p>

      <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        One thing: if you use the theme toggle, your light or dark preference is kept in your browser's local
        storage so the site remembers it next time. It never leaves your device, it identifies nothing, and
        clearing your browser data removes it.
      </p>

      <h2>Traffic statistics</h2>
      <p>
        I use <a href="https://cronitor.io/" rel="noopener">Cronitor</a> to see roughly how many people read
        what. It sets no cookies, stores no identifier on your device, does no fingerprinting, and respects
        your browser's Do Not Track setting — if you have that on, it collects nothing at all.
      </p>
      <p>
        What it does see, server-side, is the page you visited, a referrer if there was one, and your IP
        address. An IP address is personal data under GDPR, which is the reason this page exists. It is used
        to derive an approximate country and to tell one visit from another. It is not used to identify you,
        not combined with anything else, and not sold or shared.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also record two anonymous events: when someone downloads the paper, and when someone finishes the
        self-assessment. They are counts, attached to no one.
      </p>

      <h2>The self-assessment</h2>
      <p>
        Your answers never reach a server. The
        <a href="/organizational-flow/self-assessment/">self-assessment</a> runs entirely in your browser, and
        the result is encoded into the page address so you can bookmark or share it if you want to. Close the
        tab without copying the link and it is gone. Nothing is stored, and I never see your answers.
      </p>

      <h2>If you get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Email and phone go directly to me. I keep what you send for as long as the conversation is useful and
        no longer, and it goes nowhere else — no CRM, no mailing list, no newsletter to unsubscribe from,
        because there isn't one.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under GDPR you can ask what data relates to you, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, and object to
        it being processed. Given the above there is unlikely to be much to hand over, but the right stands
        and the answer will be honest. Write to
        <a href="mailto:christoffer.rasten@troi.se">christoffer.rasten@troi.se</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you think I've handled something badly and I haven't put it right, you can complain to
        <a href="https://www.imy.se/" rel="noopener">Integritetsskyddsmyndigheten</a>, the Swedish data
        protection authority. Or just contact me and we can settle it.
      </p>

      <p class="privacy-foot">
        Christoffer Råsten · TROi · <a href="mailto:christoffer.rasten@troi.se">christoffer.rasten@troi.se</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-lede { color: var(--bark); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .insight-page h2 { margin-top: 2.4rem; }
  .privacy-foot {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--mist);
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--bark);
  }
</style>
